  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Exploring Style Options**\n\nI\'ve successfully passed the linting stage with no errors. My focus has now shifted to the exciting world of MapLibre style options. I\'m currently exploring which vector tile/style provider would be ideal for this project, and I\'ve got some suggestions. Specifically, I\'m thinking of MapTiler if we don\'t already have a provider.\n\n\n**Implementing Security Practices**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing security within the threat map integration, particularly regarding sensitive data. I will leverage GeoJSON for threat and location information. Critically, I\'m setting up environment variables for map provider and API keys, ensuring that secrets are never directly exposed in the frontend code. I\'m also now thinking of ways of handling the loading and use of various dark style options, and their fallback options, which I will test and add to the system.\n\n\n**Analyzing Dark Mode Styles**\n\nI\'m now diving into the project\'s design tokens to ensure a seamless dark mode experience. I\'ve pinpointed dark backgrounds, border styles, text colors, and threat severity color codes within `src/index.css` and related files. This includes analyzing the existing use of colors like `#0b1329`, `#0f172a`, and `#020617` and the border and text values used in several components. I\'m focusing on consistency and readability within the threat map integration, ensuring that dark mode styles are clearly defined and implemented.\n\n\n**Defining Component Locations**\n\nI\'m now determining the most suitable directory structure for the map components. Considering the project\'s existing layout, I\'m leaning toward organizing within `src/features/dashboard/threat-map/` or perhaps within a dedicated `src/components/map/` directory. I\'m taking a close look at the cohesiveness of the proposed paths. I\'ve also just started outlining the look and feel of connections and arcs on the map.\n\n\n**Organizing Map Components**\n\nI\'ve decided on the directory structure. The map components will reside within `src/features/dashboard/threat-map/`. This includes `GlobalThreatMap.tsx`, `types.ts`, `mapDataAdapter.ts`, `ThreatPopup.tsx`, `MapLegend.tsx`, `MapControls.tsx`, `ThreatMapStats.tsx`, and `mapStyles.ts`. I will integrate the `GlobalThreatMap` section into `SecurityOverviewPage.tsx`. I have also reviewed the existing layout of `SecurityOverviewPage.tsx` and have re-familiarized myself with the CSS selector and the components that will host the threat map.\n\n\n**Evaluating Layout Options**\n\nI\'m now weighing alternative layouts for the dashboard\'s \"Global Threat Intelligence\" section. I\'m considering expanding it to full width or dedicating the right-hand column. I\'m focusing on user experience, and weighing how to best display a map with real-time statistics, filtering, and interactive features without overcrowding the interface. I\'m also ensuring responsiveness across various devices.\n\n\n**Refining Display Section**\n\nI\'m now fully committed to a dedicated \"Global Threat Intelligence\" section on the dashboard, as the design specifies a spacious, full-width container for the interactive map and related statistics. I\'m focusing on incorporating a \"LIVE SOC TELEMETRY\" indicator and severity filters. I\'m also planning the placement of an arc toggle.\n\n\n**Planning Map Interactions**\n\nI\'m now outlining key interactive features for the map. I plan to incorporate a summary stats bar, displaying threat locations and critical events above or beside the map. My goal is to add a large interactive canvas, incorporating a dark cybersecurity theme, custom borders, and color-coded threat markers. I am also working on adding a threat detail popup and various controls such as reset, zoom, and fullscreen functions. I also plan to add an empty state to communicate when no data is available.\n\n\n\n**Refining Widget Integration**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on integrating the \"Global Threat Intelligence\" section within `SecurityOverviewPage.tsx`. I will replace the static mini-card in the right column with a dynamic status mini-widget. I\'m considering having that widget expand into the full \"Global Threat Intelligence\" section, or placing the section right below the middle section. I\'ve re-examined the CSS selector and confirmed that the target is `div:nth-of-type(2) > div:nth-of-type(2) > div:nth-of-type(2)` which can now host this card!\n\n\n**Deciding Integration Strategy**\n\nI\'ve decided to incorporate the \"Global Threat Intelligence\" map section directly into `SecurityOverviewPage.tsx` for maximum impact, while also replacing the right-column static mini-card with a dynamic widget that links to the map. Now I\'m examining the data within `cases-store.ts` to identify seed cases. I\'m focusing on the first few cases as I plan my display.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 969446102
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
