  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the integration and resolution for the **ASHIELDER Global Threat Intelligence Map**:\n\n- **Interactive Map Engine**: Integrated **MapLibre GL** with a dark cybersecurity SOC styling palette, featuring high-contrast threat nodes, clustering with zoom expansion, and Bezier connection arcs showing cross-border attack vectors.\n- **Dynamic Telemetry Adapter**: Connected real case telemetry and investigation geolocation data directly from the cases store, with automatic fallback resolution to ensure reliable coordinate plotting without breaking the canvas.\n- **Analyst Investigation Popup**: Added interactive threat node inspection displaying defanged IoCs, Tor exit node detection, ASN details, risk scores, and a direct \"View Evidence\" deep link into the case workspace.\n- **Controls & Filtering**: Equipped the map with severity filter chips (`Critical`, `High`, `Medium`, `Low`), attack vector selectors, quick search by IP/Country/ASN/Case ID, attack arc visibility toggle, and full-screen expansion.\n- **Dashboard Integration**: Mounted the full interactive threat grid directly in the Security Overview layout, complemented by quick navigation actions from the summary cards."
    thinking: "**Reviewing Initial Development**\n\nI\'ve successfully compiled the applet without any errors! Now, I\'m reviewing the elements I\'ve built and connected. Specifically, I created `/src/features/dashboard/threat-map/types.ts`, defining a complete data contract for threat locations, GeoJSON features, and stats. I also started building a framework for other components.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed the integration and resolution for the **ASHIELDER Global Threat Intelligence Map**:\n\n- **Interactive Map Engine**: Integrated **MapLibre GL** with a dark cybersecurity SOC styling palette, featuring high-contrast threat nodes, clustering with zoom expansion, and Bezier connection arcs showing cross-border attack vectors.\n- **Dynamic Telemetry Adapter**: Connected real case telemetry and investigation geolocation data directly from the cases store, with automatic fallback resolution to ensure reliable coordinate plotting without breaking the canvas.\n- **Analyst Investigation Popup**: Added interactive threat node inspection displaying defanged IoCs, Tor exit node detection, ASN details, risk scores, and a direct \"View Evidence\" deep link into the case workspace.\n- **Controls & Filtering**: Equipped the map with severity filter chips (`Critical`, `High`, `Medium`, `Low`), attack vector selectors, quick search by IP/Country/ASN/Case ID, attack arc visibility toggle, and full-screen expansion.\n- **Dashboard Integration**: Mounted the full interactive threat grid directly in the Security Overview layout, complemented by quick navigation actions from the summary cards."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 651070407
    }
